<title>USA: Pulitzer January revenues up 16.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Pulitzer January revenues up 16.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pulitzer Publishing Co said Friday its revenues for the five weeks ended February 2 rose 16.6 percent to $48 million from $41.1 million.</p>
<p>The newspaper company said 1997 revenues included those of Scripps League Newspapers Inc (subsequently renamed Pulitzer Community Newspapers Inc), which was acquired on July 1, 1996. Pulitzer Community Newspapers added $6 million to revenues.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
